 {
  "node_id": "p69_5",
  "index": 5,
  "text": "Suppose instead we decide to consolidate all of the device interfaces into one interface that can then\nbe used to drive all appropriate devices. Given a collection of existing interfaces, we might consider\nmaking this component a wrapper that logically encapsulates the specific devices, as shown in Fig-\nure 0-28. This solution, although often employed in practice, also fails on multiple counts. Apart\nfrom having to modify the source of the output manager every time a new device comes online,\nwe impose an outrageous physical dependency: Every report writer, to be used (or even tested),\nmust link with every known output device. As if that were not bad enough, some devices (e.g., the\nWindows output device) might not exist on every supported platform! Enough said.",
  "bbox": [
   134.5,
   537.0699999999999,
   513.6049999999998,
   645.0699999999999
  ],
  "font": "HAKIBM+TimesLTPro-Roman",
